                "senderName": "NWS Salt Lake City UT",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 12 at 1:34PM MDT until October 12 at 6:00PM MDT by NWS Salt Lake City UT",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of Utah, including the following areas, Western\nMillard and Juab Counties, Bear Lake and Bear River Valley, Cache\nValley/Utah Portion, Eastern Box Elder County, Great Salt Lake\nDesert and Mountains, Northern Wasatch Front, Salt Lake Valley,\nTooele and Rush Valleys, Utah Valley, Wasatch Back, Wasatch\nMountains I-80 North, Wasatch Mountains South of I-80, Western\nUinta Basin and Western Uinta Mountains. This includes recent burn\nscars such as Rocky Canyon.\n\n* WHEN...Until 6 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and recent burn scars. Flooding may occur in poor\ndrainage and urban areas. Extensive street flooding and flooding of\ncreeks and rivers are possible.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Moisture will continue to spread into northern Utah producing a\nprolonged rainfall event. In particular, moisture interacting\nwith a frontal boundary across far northern Utah may yield\nlocally heavier rainfall totals compared to other locations. As a\nresult, areal flooding is possible across northern Utah.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.",
                "response": "Prepare",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
